1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,597
Stand up tall, reach out your hand.

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:06,797
Cut through the wind and make a stand!

3
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:11,260
The paint within brings
out a map of your own.

4
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:19,597
To the left and the right
all we saw stormy nights.

5
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,857
All the rough winds and
waves coming day after day?

6
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:28,797
And the values we had were about to
collapse Oh just where do we go next?

7
00:00:28,880 --> 00:00:35,420
And as we look down to the compass in
hand Is it showing us the right direction?

8
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,637
All we know is nobody
here knows it for certain.

9
00:00:38,720 --> 00:00:41,937
So close your eyes and breathe in deeply.

10
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:45,177
And listen to your soul.

11
00:00:45,260 --> 00:00:48,117
You'll see a path in front of you.

12
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:51,537
And you'll know just where you need to go.

13
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:55,817
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

14
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,017
Cut through the wind and make us stand.

15
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:02,880
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

16
00:01:04,620 --> 00:01:08,137
I'll do it my own way,
that's what's best for me.

17
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:11,777
And you do it your way,
that's how it's got to be.

18
00:01:11,860 --> 00:01:15,397
We're moving forward, now I'm ready.

19
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:19,217
But at times it's okay
to get help on the way.

20
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:21,757
For the future ahead, burning bright.

21
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:24,277
For what's ahead you see.

22
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:27,640
Is beyond your wildest dreams.

23
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,757
So stand up tall, reach out your hand.

24
00:01:31,840 --> 00:01:34,977
Cut through the wind and make a stand.

25
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:38,780
Don't let the darkness
win, just break through.

26
00:01:40,480 --> 00:01:44,077
We'll do it our way,
the best that we know.

27
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:45,537
With tears and doubts and tone.

28
00:01:45,620 --> 00:01:47,917
We'll go where we all wanna go.

29
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,720
The page within brings colors of our own.

30
00:01:57,260 --> 00:01:58,657
To be

31
00:01:58,740 --> 00:02:05,740
continued...

32
00:02:31,660 --> 00:02:34,220
Hurry, this way! Yeah!

33
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,280
Damn, we're trapped here.

34
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:44,230
You're right.

35
00:02:44,313 --> 00:02:46,613
The heat will kill us before we get out.

36
00:02:54,300 --> 00:02:55,600
Yes, this is it!

37
00:03:07,880 --> 00:03:11,080
You're Jinbei from the
Straw Hats! Thank you!

38
00:03:11,320 --> 00:03:12,660
You're really strong!

39
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:14,377
Head the opposite way.

40
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,401
The fire hasn't spread there yet.

41
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:18,740
Just focus on surviving.

42
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:20,170
All right.

43
00:03:20,260 --> 00:03:21,557
We'll save ourselves.

44
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:25,220
You stay safe too! Right! Now go!

45
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:27,170
Yeah!

46
00:03:27,253 --> 00:03:28,160
You heard the man!

47
00:03:42,080 --> 00:03:44,380
Why did the flames spread so quickly?

48
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:47,666
It's one thing for a
warrior to die in battle,

49
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:51,198
but this fire will cause so
many needless casualties!

50
00:04:05,340 --> 00:04:07,800
It's too dangerous to stay here now.

51
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:10,320
We need to run to some place safer.

52
00:04:14,280 --> 00:04:16,020
Is something wrong, Doctor?

53
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:21,000
Fighting for a nation!

54
00:04:41,540 --> 00:04:43,480
She's back!

55
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:44,970
Yay!

56
00:04:45,053 --> 00:04:45,883
Oh, Doctor!

57
00:04:45,966 --> 00:04:47,020
I'm so glad!

58
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:48,920
And as an added bonus,

59
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:53,416
now you, Karoo, know the side effects
of your extended gigantification.

60
00:04:53,520 --> 00:04:57,880
Yeah, I thought something might
happen, but I didn't expect that.

61
00:04:59,060 --> 00:05:00,480
It's a fair payoff.

62
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:05,320
I'm stronger and bigger for longer,
but weaker and smaller once it's over.

63
00:05:05,740 --> 00:05:09,681
But that reminds me there's someone
else dealing with side effects.

64
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:13,920
Miyagi, I'm worried
about how Zoro's doing.

65
00:05:14,500 --> 00:05:17,400
Indeed, it won't be pretty.

66
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:22,449
He had 20 or 30 bones broken and had
countless other injuries on top of that.

67
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:26,449
The medicine healed him instantly,
but doesn't last forever.

68
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:29,160
When it's done, he'll hurt twice as bad?

69
00:05:30,560 --> 00:05:31,390
Yeah.

70
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:34,724
Those wounds were bad
enough in the first place.

71
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:39,760
Zoro, you better not die.

72
00:06:27,940 --> 00:06:29,175
Who the hell are you?

73
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,680
What do you want?

74
00:06:40,500 --> 00:06:45,200
Hey, no, what the hell's
going on, I can't,

75
00:06:45,620 --> 00:06:49,260
I can't move, stay back, don't do it, no!

76
00:06:56,120 --> 00:06:58,280
Out of my way!

77
00:07:09,240 --> 00:07:10,917
I ain't got time for this crap!

78
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,118
I gotta find Zoro!

79
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,180
This isn't fair.

80
00:07:23,360 --> 00:07:26,097
We had this till one of
Whitemir's commanders stepped in.

81
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:29,239
Why the hell is he hoping
Straw Hat and the Samurai?

82
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:49,660
I'm a sloppy.

83
00:07:50,700 --> 00:07:53,288
The peace pirates aren't
to be trifled with.

84
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:57,280
Kaku, keep him up.

85
00:07:57,720 --> 00:07:58,740
It's fine.

86
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:00,273
As long as you're safe.

87
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,620
Cypher-pull.

88
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:18,720
Indeed, we're Aegis Zero.

89
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:21,320
I was afraid this might happen.

90
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:26,300
Izo, we never saw each other.

91
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:31,960
To be clear, the Whitebeard pilots
committed a historical crime.

92
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:34,671
That's not something we can simply ignore.

93
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:39,740
But our business is with the Straw Hats,
and that is more than enough for now.

94
00:08:42,120 --> 00:08:44,100
I'm sure we'll meet again.

95
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:51,980
We are not done here.

96
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:53,960
CP Zero.

97
00:09:05,220 --> 00:09:06,800
Just a little more.

98
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,240
I can still make it!

99
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:15,120
Don't you dare!

100
00:09:19,180 --> 00:09:21,260
Wearing all hands.

101
00:09:22,500 --> 00:09:24,900
And slips into the rain.

102
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:28,220
Don't do that! Come on!

103
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:29,540
What is your deal?

104
00:09:41,280 --> 00:09:42,110
Namuji!

105
00:09:43,120 --> 00:09:44,560
Place your fight!

106
00:09:59,020 --> 00:10:04,260
If that thing so much as touches those
explosives, everything will be over.

107
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:10,009
I don't know where you came
from, but you can go right back!

108
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,050
Mahoropa!

109
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:56,580
That's enough, Big Mom! Please!

110
00:10:56,880 --> 00:10:58,586
They can't even move anymore!

111
00:10:58,760 --> 00:10:59,960
You've won, okay?

112
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:02,087
You don't have to kill them!

113
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:04,680
Come on!

114
00:11:04,860 --> 00:11:06,040
I'm begging you!

115
00:11:12,900 --> 00:11:15,340
Even your own men are pitying you.

116
00:11:15,600 --> 00:11:18,306
It's not a good look for
the worst generation.

117
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:23,060
Hey, hurry up! Hmm?

118
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,880
They want this by us!

119
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,237
Just run out a little
longer and we'll save you!

120
00:11:28,320 --> 00:11:31,857
