243
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:15,077
Stupid brat.

244
00:21:15,160 --> 00:21:16,900
You must learn your place.

245
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:20,620
Mother's visit. Cannon!

246
00:21:21,620 --> 00:21:24,700
Three thousand leagues of misery!

247
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:51,340
What the hell is that thing?

248
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:13,420
You can't escape me!

249
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:35,340
Our attack is chasing us down.

250
00:22:35,680 --> 00:22:36,600
It's alive!

251
00:23:06,460 --> 00:23:08,840
Ma-ma-ma-ma-ma!

252
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:11,780
Time to finish them all!

253
00:23:13,760 --> 00:23:16,520
Put those little punks
in the ground, Misery!

254
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:21,740
Now tucked!

255
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:49,880
K-Room.

256
00:23:50,340 --> 00:23:51,720
K-Room.

257
00:24:01,560 --> 00:24:04,120
This trick I can't revolve her!

258
00:24:08,800 --> 00:24:10,380
Is that a sword?

259
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:22,540
You'll pay for that.

260
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:28,037
You've got some balls on you!

261
00:24:28,120 --> 00:24:31,040
How long did you sit
here to hold on to me?

262
00:24:37,660 --> 00:24:38,617
Captain, no!

263
00:24:38,700 --> 00:24:42,440
What are you doing, Captain?
Let go! You're gonna die!

264
00:24:42,660 --> 00:24:43,940
It's not worth it!

265
00:24:48,560 --> 00:24:49,780
Deeper. Deeper.

266
00:24:49,940 --> 00:24:51,220
Just a little more.

267
00:24:52,600 --> 00:24:53,820
This is pointless.

268
00:24:54,320 --> 00:24:57,085
You really wanted me to
beat you to death, huh?

269
00:25:06,400 --> 00:25:07,480
Now puncture.

270
00:25:08,700 --> 00:25:09,530
Huh?

271
00:25:09,613 --> 00:25:11,820
What are you doing? Fall!

272
00:25:38,700 --> 00:25:39,641
What's going on?

273
00:25:40,600 --> 00:25:41,520
A giant hole?

274
00:25:42,500 --> 00:25:43,971
Where did that come from?

275
00:26:01,100 --> 00:26:02,806
What are they doing up there?

276
00:26:08,700 --> 00:26:10,580
Burn him to ash, Misery!

277
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:15,200
Eustass! Do it already!

278
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:18,430
What's that?

279
00:26:18,900 --> 00:26:21,220
Telling me what to do again, Trafalgar!

280
00:26:21,460 --> 00:26:23,820
Just sit there and keep your mouth shut!

281
00:26:34,840 --> 00:26:36,460
You're gonna ship me!

282
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:45,700
I'm not scared of you, you nasty boy.

283
00:26:45,940 --> 00:26:47,058
Give me your worst.

284
00:26:47,300 --> 00:26:49,080
You can't beat Big Mom.

285
00:26:50,340 --> 00:26:52,300
Keep telling yourself that.

286
00:26:53,760 --> 00:26:56,480
Now jump. Mom!

287
00:26:57,880 --> 00:26:59,520
You don't rule in our era.

288
00:27:01,720 --> 00:27:03,120
Your time sucks.

289
00:27:22,360 --> 00:27:25,620
You pulled out all the stops this time.

290
00:27:26,400 --> 00:27:28,480
Honestly, I'm impressed.

291
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:37,120
You boys must really like me.

292
00:27:38,800 --> 00:27:41,460
You don't want our time together to end,

293
00:27:41,640 --> 00:27:44,346
even though you can
barely stand on your feet.

294
00:27:44,740 --> 00:27:46,400
You're young, of course,

295
00:27:46,680 --> 00:27:52,580
and you've got lots of energy, but I'm
made of much sterner stuff than you.

296
00:27:53,140 --> 00:27:56,217
You flats probably thought
you'd driven me to the brink,

297
00:27:56,300 --> 00:27:59,420
but try as you might, you can't defeat me!

298
00:28:02,640 --> 00:28:03,800
She's not dead?

299
00:28:03,980 --> 00:28:05,537
What the hell is it gonna take?

300
00:28:05,620 --> 00:28:09,444
They've been kicking her ass, but
now she's just laughing at all.

301
00:28:09,620 --> 00:28:10,800
Come on, boss!

302
00:28:11,940 --> 00:28:13,160
This is insane!

303
00:28:14,300 --> 00:28:16,359
Kid and the captain are both spent.

304
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:17,310
We're screwed!

305
00:28:18,040 --> 00:28:23,680
And when I do, your miserable little
life will be putty in my hands.

306
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:26,020
I'll grant you what mercy.

307
00:28:26,400 --> 00:28:28,580
You may choose your punishment.

308
00:28:29,240 --> 00:28:32,977
Would you like to hand over
50 years of your lifespan?

309
00:28:33,060 --> 00:28:37,380
Or would you rather stay
as you are and be my slave?

310
00:28:41,160 --> 00:28:44,900
Will it be life or slave?

311
00:28:49,120 --> 00:28:51,220
You took so much ass!

312
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:53,020
That's enough, boss!

313
00:28:53,260 --> 00:28:54,420
We gotta book it!

314
00:28:56,980 --> 00:28:58,260
It's not fair!

315
00:28:58,420 --> 00:28:59,817
She's taking her life pants too!

316
00:28:59,900 --> 00:29:02,420
Stop it! Hi, boy! Hi, boy!

317
00:29:08,080 --> 00:29:08,910
No!

318
00:29:08,993 --> 00:29:10,540
Don't say anything but this!

319
00:29:14,640 --> 00:29:18,640
I thought she was going to die,
then she turns around and does this!

320
00:29:18,760 --> 00:29:20,020
She's a monster!

321
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:22,460
You've got to run!

322
00:29:22,840 --> 00:29:24,487
Get away from here, Captain!

323
00:29:32,600 --> 00:29:33,980
You guys should run.

324
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:36,780
What a joke.

325
00:29:37,060 --> 00:29:38,354
She thinks I'm scared.

326
00:29:40,020 --> 00:29:42,280
Now I'm not giving you a damn thing.

327
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:44,800
And I'll never be your slave.

328
00:29:45,320 --> 00:29:46,820
This is just a bluff.

329
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:50,386
You've got one foot in
the grave, you old hag,

330
00:29:50,500 --> 00:29:53,324
and your half-assed threats
don't intimidate me!

331
00:29:55,660 --> 00:29:57,137
I can't believe it!

332
00:29:57,220 --> 00:30:00,514
Not even a second of their
lifespan has been taken away!

333
00:30:00,740 --> 00:30:02,387
She's an emperor on the sea!

334
00:30:02,520 --> 00:30:05,108
You're telling me they're
not scared at all?

335
00:30:08,940 --> 00:30:09,770
Roronoa.

336
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:13,612
As much as I'd like to relish my victory,

337
00:30:14,020 --> 00:30:16,373
the dying screams will probably ruin it.

338
00:30:16,780 --> 00:30:18,180
Unless I do this.

339
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:21,240
A gift from the man who saved me.

340
00:30:25,620 --> 00:30:29,120
Stop being such a sore loser
and take a hit, damn it!

341
00:30:29,340 --> 00:30:31,140
The Underworld is waiting!

342
00:30:31,560 --> 00:30:34,180
Let me help you on your way! It's silence!

343
00:30:37,880 --> 00:30:38,710
Huh?

344
00:30:38,793 --> 00:30:40,622
Is something wrong with my ears?

345
00:30:47,580 --> 00:30:48,880
Scream into the void.

346
00:30:49,160 --> 00:30:50,278
We've heard enough.

347
00:30:51,240 --> 00:30:53,416
This technique cancels out all sound.

348
00:30:57,760 --> 00:30:59,660
Sorry, didn't catch that.

349
00:31:00,020 --> 00:31:01,120
What's happening?

350
00:31:01,460 --> 00:31:02,740
My voice is gone!

351
00:31:04,480 --> 00:31:06,760
Captain, look behind you!

352
00:31:09,640 --> 00:31:11,960
And one more for the road!

353
00:31:12,620 --> 00:31:13,450
Jack!

354
00:31:44,380 --> 00:31:45,780
Prometheus!

355
00:31:47,200 --> 00:31:48,600
Hera!

356
00:31:51,460 --> 00:31:52,290
Anna!

357
00:31:52,373 --> 00:31:53,257
What are you doing?

358
00:31:53,340 --> 00:31:56,040
Why aren't you helping me?

359
00:31:59,580 --> 00:32:00,460
What?

360
00:32:00,900 --> 00:32:02,120
That big mom!

361
00:32:04,820 --> 00:32:06,160
What happened?

362
00:32:06,480 --> 00:32:07,656
Everything's silent!

363
00:32:09,680 --> 00:32:12,580
Nothing I touch makes the sound!

364
00:32:13,300 --> 00:32:17,360
What the hell have you done
to me, Trafalder? Whoa!

365
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:18,660
Let it go!

366
00:32:28,560 --> 00:32:29,660
It's gone!

367
00:32:49,520 --> 00:32:50,350
What?

368
00:32:50,433 --> 00:32:52,020
Is that smoke?

369
00:32:52,460 --> 00:32:53,860
What's going on?

370
00:32:55,860 --> 00:32:58,360
Curse those stupid brats!

371
00:32:58,860 --> 00:33:01,600
And curse you too, Roger!

372
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:08,820
You just couldn't keep your mouth shut!

373
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:13,480
Why the hell did you have to go
and say that before you died?

374
00:33:18,640 --> 00:33:20,580
So you all want my treasure?

375
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:22,979
Well, you can go ahead and have it.

376
00:33:23,980 --> 00:33:25,140
It's out there.

377
00:33:26,440 --> 00:33:28,400
I left it in one place.

378
00:33:28,560 --> 00:33:30,266
Now you just have to find it.

379
00:33:35,700 --> 00:33:37,400
People ain't bad up.

380
00:33:37,680 --> 00:33:39,640
The whole world bought into it.

381
00:33:46,540 --> 00:33:52,540
Great pirate era but what do you care
you're dead it's not your problem is it?

382
00:33:59,760 --> 00:34:04,580
All these brats got fired up
thanks to your little speech Roger!

383
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:12,097
And the pirates you left behind from your

384
00:34:12,180 --> 00:34:15,298
generation we're the ones
who have to deal with them.

385
00:34:36,360 --> 00:34:38,380
That doesn't sound good!

386
00:34:38,780 --> 00:34:40,460
We need to leave now!

387
00:34:41,200 --> 00:34:42,600
Is there anyone there?

388
00:34:43,560 --> 00:34:45,257
What was that noise?

389
00:34:45,340 --> 00:34:47,600
Someone answer me!

390
00:35:16,100 --> 00:35:16,930
Otter!

391
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:25,780
It's not fair, Otter.

392
00:35:26,240 --> 00:35:29,300
You should have told us
before you left this world.

393
00:35:29,640 --> 00:35:31,000
The One Piece.

394
00:35:32,200 --> 00:35:34,360
Is the treasure even real?

395
00:35:35,780 --> 00:35:37,140
What is it?

396
00:35:37,620 --> 00:35:39,000
Where is it?

397
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:44,200
It could be right beneath my
nose and I wouldn't have a clue.

398
00:35:45,800 --> 00:35:47,760
It's so frustrating!

399
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:01,200
Kid!

400
00:36:02,580 --> 00:36:03,410
Look!

401
00:36:03,660 --> 00:36:06,120
You won't get away with this.

402
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:08,460
My story isn't over.

403
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:09,960
It can't be.

404
00:36:10,240 --> 00:36:11,840
Not like this, dammit.

405
00:36:12,160 --> 00:36:13,957
I won't die.

406
00:36:14,040 --> 00:36:15,780
Not from this!

407
00:36:16,080 --> 00:36:20,580
Mark my words, I will be back!

408
00:36:33,040 --> 00:36:37,687
The battle between Emperor of the Sea
Big Mom and the New Generation has ended.

409
00:36:40,260 --> 00:36:43,417
On the performance floor inside the skull

410
00:36:43,500 --> 00:36:47,080
dome a cheer rings out
the winners are clear

411
00:36:53,960 --> 00:36:58,120
After a desperate struggle
Eustass captain kid

412
00:36:59,900 --> 00:37:03,317
And his ally the surgeon of death

413
00:37:03,400 --> 00:37:08,360
Trafalgar Law are victorious at last.

414
00:37:08,720 --> 00:37:11,040
You did it, boss!

415
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:14,320
Captain!

416
00:37:15,680 --> 00:37:17,280
You beat a new prophecy!

417
00:37:18,260 --> 00:37:19,520
This is a big deal!

418
00:37:19,680 --> 00:37:21,440
A really big deal!

419
00:37:38,560 --> 00:37:39,390
I see.

420
00:37:39,473 --> 00:37:40,397
So it's you.

421
00:37:40,480 --> 00:37:42,020
But why have you come?

422
00:37:48,920 --> 00:37:49,817
All right.

423
00:37:49,900 --> 00:37:51,724
This will do for now, at least.

424
00:37:53,140 --> 00:37:53,970
Wow!

425
00:37:54,053 --> 00:37:56,760
I knew you could do it,
Momonosuke! Keep it up!

426
00:37:58,280 --> 00:37:59,377
Yamato, it's you!

427
00:37:59,460 --> 00:38:02,000
Is that the basement? Oh no!

428
00:38:02,340 --> 00:38:03,380
It's exposed!

429
00:38:04,180 --> 00:38:05,680
It's been a real mess.

430
00:38:05,900 --> 00:38:07,547
Big Mom just set off a bomb.

431
00:38:07,740 --> 00:38:09,269
It blew out half the wall.

432
00:38:10,200 --> 00:38:11,777
I saw the explosion earlier.

433
00:38:11,860 --> 00:38:13,625
So that was her doing, was it?

434
00:38:14,240 --> 00:38:15,070
Uh-huh.

435
00:38:15,180 --> 00:38:17,257
I'm lucky the whole armory didn't explode.

436
00:38:17,340 --> 00:38:20,987
I was able to freeze everything,
so we should be safe for now.

437
00:38:22,120 --> 00:38:22,950
That's good news.

438
00:38:23,033 --> 00:38:25,195
I'm glad to see that you are unharmed.

439
00:38:26,580 --> 00:38:30,521
I'm still fighting to do my part,
but I need to tell you something.

440
00:38:31,660 --> 00:38:34,057
We have a very large visitor coming.

441
00:38:34,140 --> 00:38:38,857
Are you familiar with
Zunesha the giant elephant

442
00:38:38,940 --> 00:38:41,777
the same one Odin wrote
about in his journal?

443
00:38:41,860 --> 00:38:43,160
Impossible. Papa!

444
00:38:58,560 --> 00:39:03,000
Zunesha was a companion of Joy Boy
who committed a crime 800 years ago.

445
00:39:03,560 --> 00:39:05,000
What could it all mean?
